# ============================================================================
# Chatimall — Frontend Environment Template
# ============================================================================
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values.
# NEVER commit the real .env file.
#
# Vercel: set these in the dashboard (Project Settings -> Environment Variables).
# They are embedded in the production build at build time, so after changing any
# VITE_* variable you must REDEPLOY the frontend for the change to take effect.
# ============================================================================

# ---- API server ------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave EMPTY during browser local development. Vite automatically proxies:
#   /api/*       -> http://localhost:4000
#   /socket.io/* -> ws://localhost:4000
#
# For Vercel deploys, Android APK builds, or any hosting that isn't local:
# set this to your backend's FULL public URL (no trailing slash).
#
# This MUST be set on Vercel as an Environment Variable (Project Settings ->
# Environment Variables -> add VITE_API_URL as Plaintext, check Production +
# Preview boxes, save, then REDEPLOY — VITE_* vars are baked in at build time).
#
# YOUR live backend (deployed 2026-10-12 on Render free tier):
#   https://chatimall-backend-4.onrender.com
#
# Uncomment and set the correct value below, or better yet, set it in the
# Vercel dashboard so it never gets accidentally committed.
# VITE_API_URL=https://chatimall-backend-4.onrender.com

# ---- WebRTC TURN relay (optional, recommended for mobile calls) -----------
# Only needed if 1:1 video/voice calls fail on strict mobile/office networks
# that block peer-to-peer UDP STUN. Twilio, Xirsys, Open Relay Project, etc.
# VITE_TURN_URL=turn:turn.yourserver.com:3478
# VITE_TURN_USERNAME=
# VITE_TURN_CREDENTIAL=
